# Weekly KISS audit (operator ruling 2026-10-08: guard simplicity).
# One read-only Claude run lists what the last 7 days added to system and the
# pack: new commands, flags, config keys, state stores, files, documents, and
# net lines. It files one sd item when it finds any; the dashboard shows it.
# Step 2 files one item to retire skills unused for 60 days (ruling
# #58341, operator 2026-11-16).
JOB_SCHEDULE="0 7 * * 1"
JOB_TIMEOUT="30m"
JOB_COMMAND=". \"\$HOME/.config/shell/env.sh\" >/dev/null 2>&1; cd \"$ROOT/..\" && claude -p 'KISS audit and weekly grill seed, read-only. Window: the last 7 days. 1. For this system checkout (the working directory) and ~/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow, read git log and diffs of origin/main in the window. List each new command or subcommand (a command is an executable a user runs, such as an extensionless bin/ file; a bin/*.py library module is not one), flag, config key, state store, gate or check, file kind and document, with the commit; and net lines per repo, counting the pack dashboard/ apart from the rest of the pack. 2. Run sd skill list. Take each skill whose last use is more than 60 days ago, or never used and in contrib/ for more than 60 days (standing rule, grill sd:9044 #57885). If any, run exactly one: sd task add --priority 3 --belongs-to $HOME/repos/platypeeps/sd-workflow --ref skill-retire:<YYYY-MM-DD> --body <one line each: retire skill <name>, last <date or never>> Retire skills unused 60 days: week to <date>. 3. Run sd-db repo list; take the rows whose third field is yes. For each, run git -C <path> ls-tree --name-only origin/HEAD README.md CLAUDE.md .claude/rules and list each missing one: <repo> misses <file>; list a missing .claude/rules only when CLAUDE.md has more than 100 lines (ruling #40946). For a repo under ~/repos/research/ check README.md only. Then run git -C <path> log origin/HEAD --since=7.days --diff-filter=A --name-only --format= -- docs/work/ and list each added prd.md: <repo> starts new work in prd.md: <path>. If the lists are not empty, run exactly one: sd task add --priority 3 --ref grill:<YYYY-MM-DD> --body <the lists, one line each> KISS audit and grill: week to <date>. Then file at most 10 seed questions on that item, drawn from the new mechanisms, the drift above, lane entries sd today shows running or pending for more than a day, and rulings a commit in the window contradicts. One sd task note <item> --kind question call each; its body is the question, then a line Option: <recommended> (Recommended) and a line Option: <other>. Change nothing else.' --model sonnet --allowedTools 'Bash(git -C:*) Bash(git log:*) Bash(git diff:*) Bash(sd task add:*) Bash(sd task note:*) Bash(sd skill list:*) Bash(sd-db repo list:*) Bash(sd today:*) Read Grep Glob' < /dev/null"
